\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, let us join our friends above
\par That have obtained the prize,
\par And on the eagle wings of love
\par To joys celestial rise:
\par Let all the saints terrestrial sing,
\par With those to glory gone;
\par For all the servants of our King,
\par In earth and heaven are one.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. One family we dwell in Him,
\par One Church, above, beneath,
\par Though now divided by the stream,
\par The narrow stream of death:
\par One army of the living God,
\par To His command we bow;
\par Part of His host have crossed the flood,
\par And part are crossing now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Ten thousand to their endless home
\par This solemn moment fly;
\par And we are to the margin come,
\par And we expect to die;
\par Even now by faith we join our hands
\par With those that went before,
\par And greet the blood-besprinkled bands
\par On the eternal shore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Our spirits too shall quickly join,
\par Like theirs with glory crowned,
\par And shout to see our Captain's sign,
\par To hear His trumpet sound
\par O that we now might grasp our Guide!
\par O that the word were given!
\par Come, Lord of hosts, the waves divide,
\par And land us all in heaven.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

